WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.400
The only thing we'll help you with is the panning;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.110
the actual execution of the plan is up to you, the client.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.030
Understood?

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.650
Then the negotiations are concluded.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.160
Don’t forget the special fee you owe us when
the crime is successfully concluded.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.370
House of Illusion Murders.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.420
Then Gotouda-san, please show me this letter.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.310
Yes

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.170
This threatening letter was sent to
the mountain villa of my teacher,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:14.470
Japan’s most famous violinist,
Masaomi, two weeks ago.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.520
“Sensei’s violin is mine.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.680
I will hand it to no one.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.480
With death, I shall prove this.”

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.730
A handwritten letter?

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.780
Yes.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.290
And who is that?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.160
Yuge-sensei’s best student, Houshou Mitsuru.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.210
But she committed suicide six months ago.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.760
With only a little while left before
Sensei's illness ends his life,

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.590
he's gathered his students and critics at his villa,

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.850
and said that he would decide who
to give his treasured violin to there.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:03.560
But he’s worried that something may happen then.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.400
Treasured violin?

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:13.030
Yes. The Testa di Drago. It's Italian;
it means “Dragon's Head".

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.250
A maestro back from the dead?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.220
Uh... What is a maestro?

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.920
A name given to supremely talented musicians.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.420
I've explained the nature of the job,
but let me add one more thing.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:34.760
The man who made that violin is the man
who made this old school building,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.140
and the man who made the trick on that secret door.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.180
You can’t mean...

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:41.520
Yes.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.940
Kuzuryuu Takumi.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.950
He was a genius at all things, and his
works are collected around the world.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:59.240
He made nine violins that were said to be
Superior even to the famed Stradivarius.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:01.950
Nine?

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:05.620
That’s the nine in Kuzuryuu.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.460
He never made ten of the same item.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:18.220
One of the masterpieces that genius made was
the Testa di Drago, worth several million yen.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.060
Now then, the“ones who will be
gong to the house will

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.780
Let me do it.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.320
Yes.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.110
Then Ryuu, Minami and Kyuu.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.230
Yes.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.910
Narusawa-kun, you stay at the school and analyze
the data brought by the members on the ground.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:45.080
And Touyama, you will provide a
guard for the client, Gotouda,

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.250
who will be returning late to the mansion.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.580
GOT IT!

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.340
Then good luck, Q-Class!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.340
Right!

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.050
Welcome, DDS.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.640
Welcome to this house of illusions.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.060
I am Yuge Masaomi.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.390
It must have been hard to make it to a villa
all the way out here in the mountains.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:07.980
Not at all.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.190
Excuse us.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.780
Oh? Where’s Gotouda-kun?

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.530
Aren’t you with him?

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:21.240
Gotouda-kun will come later with another DDS member.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.450
Jeez, Gotouda, that piece of trash.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:28.830
He’s in charge of taking care of Yuge sensei,
and on a day as important as this, he's late?

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.210
Now now, Kirishima-kun. ..

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.640
He's a student too.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:40.180
Surrounded by people such as yourselves, he
doesn’t stand out nearly as much, though.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.470
Well, I hear there’s a typhoon coming.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.060
Even if something happens between
us, the police can't get here easily.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:50.560
Murasame, what are you saying?

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:51.860
Nothing, really.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.230
They don’t seem to get along.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.900
Yeah.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.780
Oh, don’t worry about it.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:04.990
We may not look like it, but once we start
playing, we can work in perfect harmony.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.460
That’s quite right,

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:12.420
Houshu Mitsuru is probably nodding
in her grave right now.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.710
Houshu Mitsuru, huh?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.920
If that unparalleled genius of a violinist was still alive,

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.090
this discord never would've happened.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:29.690
But somebody who’s dead can’t inherit the Testa di Drago.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.230
Umm, Yuge-sensei.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.440
What is it, Arisa-kun?

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.820
The guest's rooms are ready.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.490
WAS

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.620
This is your room, Kyuu-san and Ryuu-san

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.540
Please use the one next door, Minami-san.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:49.790
All right! The attic!

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.920
I’m sorry this is all we have for you.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:59.720
Arisa-san, does Yuge-sensei intend to give the
Testa di Drago to one of his students?

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.340
That's not necessarily true, I think.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.760
Then it's possible that he won't give it to them?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.850
Fukuoka, the music critic, is Sensei’s good friend.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:15.150
He may keep it until a suitable violinist appears.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:20.860
And Shiba-sama the collector has offered
to pay 700 million yen for it.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.700
Now that Houshu Mitsuru in dead,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.330
I don’t know if there’s anybody
who can be called his successor.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.910
I just don’t know.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:39.050
There will be a solo performance from Yuge-sensei's
Testa di Drago in the orchestra hall at 5

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.220
Everyone, please come to see it.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:52.020
It is now 4 PM and the typhoon is getting
extremely strong while heading northeast.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.690
This is a REALLY bad storm, isn’t it, Sensei?

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.400
Dammit! show SOME kind of reaction, would you?

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.700
Why do I have to be with him?

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.330
It’s almost time for the solo.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:18.130
Listen then, sinful musicians, to the
melody of Hell’s Maestro!

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:29.260
Well, it’s almost a waste that you laymen get to listen
first-hand to the melodies of the master, Yuge Masaomi.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:31.890
Huh?

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.730
Shirase-san isn’t here yet.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:14.310
That violin is the Testa di Drago.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.330
I don’t know what it is, but it sounds amazing!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.380
It’s like my soul’s being drawn out.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:54.470
Sanshima Station

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.470
Amazing! I’ve never heard anything like this!

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.850
But Kirishima-san left halfway through, didn’t he?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.350
Maybe he had to go to the bathroom?

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:28.940
How can you say something so vulgar in a place like this?

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.530
Perhaps he lost his self-confidence?

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.740
To the still unparalleled playing of Yuge-sensei...

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:40.830
And that song was “The Demon’s Banquet”, too

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:42.670
“The Demon’s Banquet”?

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.460
Now then, I'll be on my way.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.060
That was quite a performance.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.220
Kirishima-san was weird too, but I wonder what
it was that happened with Shirase-san.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:58.180
Yeah.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.400
It sounds like something shattered.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.490
Where’s it coming from?

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:19.830
Downstairs, it seems like.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:21.700
Let’s go.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:24.620
What’s wrong, Shirase-san?

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.620
Open up!

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.080
What’s going on?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:28.880
ls something wrong?

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:30.340
This is strange.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.460
Where’s the room key?

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:33.170
This is it?

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.380
Hey, what’s wrong?

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:39.430
It won’t open.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.480
There’s a big shard of a pot caught on it.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.100
Let’s both push it.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:45.520
All right!

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:01.290
What is this?

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:03.750
Shiese,

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.000
The track on the CD changed.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:10.960
This is the same song we just heard!

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:12.880
"The Demon’s Banquet”.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.840
Houshou Mitsuru’s best song!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.510
Houshou Mitsuru.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:35.740
Kirishima-san!

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.950
This song!

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.750
Everyone, please stay out of of the crime scene.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.330
Megu, I’m going to investigate. You record.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.130
Yeah.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.960
Hey guys, over here.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.380
The window’s open, and it looks like rain fell on the floor.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.720
The criminal escaped from this window.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:58.390
Considering that the door didn’t
open at first, you must be right.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.180
But wouldn’t they be soaked?

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:03.890
Nobody looked wet.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.350
They just needed to get a raincoat ready.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.560
Wait.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:12.940
You guys are talking like the criminal is one of us,

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.160
but a thief may have come in from outside!

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.280
I don’t think that’s true.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:19.870
There’s no footprints.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:24.540
If it was an outsider who came through all
this rain, there should be muddy footprints.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.540
It’s possible that they changed their shoes,

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:32.510
but if that was what they were doing then they
probably would’ve been more quiet too.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:37.720
It’s most likely that somebody here did it.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.350
Prank phone calls every day at the same time?

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.640
That’s really creepy.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:48.360
Gotouda-san, any idea who did it?

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:53.690
No. Just that I heard the faint sound
of a violin on the other end.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:54.820
Violin?

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:02.490
“The Demon’s Banquet”?

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:05.870
I have a CD of hers right here.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.210
Wow, she’s pretty cute.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.170
Why would she kill herself?

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:20.970
Well, actually we never found her body.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:28.810
Her room in a villa at the edge of the
cape was stained right red with blood.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.230
It was awful.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.650
The blood continued to the outside terrace,

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:39.490
so the police surmised that she cut her wrists and
then jumped into the ocean from the terrace.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:41.780
They haven’t found the body?

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:46.460
Then it's possible that she was alive,
and that she sent those letters.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:52.380
But if she was alive, wouldn’t she
been sure to get the Testa di Drago?

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:59.680
Before she killed herself, she became
unable to play the violin.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.850
This is Touyama.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:10.770
Megu?

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:13.990
What?

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.440
What's wrong?

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:21.070
A student of Yuge-Sensai named Shirase
Mayumi was just murdered.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:23.740
Shirase-san was?

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:27.080
Dammit! Are we at the house of illusions yet?

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.040
Calm down, Touyama!

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.040
How can I calm down when there’s been a murder?

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.750
More importantly, let’s deduce what we can from here!

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.560
This is...

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.440
Touyama, look at this.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.200
Part of a timer.

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:04.320
Does that mean that this landslide
was caused by Hell’s Maestro?

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.370
The road is completely cut off.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:08.700
We'll have to walk.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.880
That song I tried so hard to avoid...

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:19.090
Houshu Mitsuru’s “The Demon’s Banquet”!

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:29.850
This is Kirishima.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:38.820
Understood.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:39.530
Bye.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.320
A landslide?

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.110
What are they going to do?

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.660
Walk, they say.

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:49.490
But they said that the landslide was
caused deliberately with dynamite.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.830
Who did it?

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:54.750
No, more importantly, why did
they do something like that?

00:17:55.690 --> 00:18:02.670
Could the “Hell’s Maestro” who killed
Shirase intend to kill again?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.090
No way!

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:12.020
To think we’d have to walk for several hours in this rain.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.600
Shall I carry your luggage?

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.980
It’s just my violin and one bag.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:23.280
Six, huh?

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.950
It'll be late at night before we get there.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.530
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.830
I hope nothing else happens.

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:37.500
Kirishima-san, where are you going in this rain?

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.250
Shut up!

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:39.880
Is something wrong?

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.130
I finished getting dinner ready and was about
to call everybody, when I saw Kirishima. ..

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.130
I don’t need food.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:47.510
I’m going home!

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.760
I can’t stay in this haunted house anymore!

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.640
Haunted house?

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:57.690
We all heard a loud noise and ran to see
what happened, and Shirase was dead!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:19:02.860
If it wasn’t a ghost, then who could have killed her?

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:05.030
It wasn’t everyone.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:11.030
There’s one person who had the time to do it.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.500
Yuge-sensei was a little late. He could’ve done it.

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:22.590
Amakusa-san, that's too much!

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:24.050
He's sick!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.970
Aren’t you the suspicious one?

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:34.100
Amakusa-kun, your eyes were wild
heard sensei’s song.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:40.480
Kirishima-kun, are you heading out?

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.020
You can’t go anywhere.

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:44.190
What do you mean?

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.690
Something terrible has happened!

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:57.120
The only road out.

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:01.170
It’s a curse.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.340
We’re cursed.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.300
By Hell’s Maestro,

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.090
Houshou Mitsuru!

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:09.340
Kirishima-san!

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:13.010
Kyuu, Megu, look up there where it fell from.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:17.730
Don’t you think that’s an unnatural shape for an landslide?

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:22.940
When there’s a landslide, dirt loosened
by the rain slides down.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.110
There shouldn’t be a hole like that!

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:29.860
This is the same thing that happened to Kinta!

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:33.370
We’re trapped in the house of illusions.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:40.830
I'm sure none of you are hungry after what just happened,

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.130
but let us eat.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:46.420
You're going to eat alone after we're
done again, Murasame-kun?

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:50.630
At a time like this, at least, you should eat with everyone.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.390
Yeah.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:56.470
Artists are finicky about things like
that, but he’s worse than usual.

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.350
Worse?

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.980
He has other things?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.980
Yeah. Like he'll always take a shower three times a day,

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.360
or drink two glasses of whiskey after dinner,

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:11.490
or always shake up a drink, no matter
what it is, before he opens it.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:12.740
Lots of things,

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:16.540
Murasame-kun is actually quite obsessive-compulsive.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:19.830
I don’t feel like eating.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:20.870
See you

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.080
You've barely eaten anything!

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:26.420
Where’s Arisa-san?

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:30.300
She said that she’d eat by herself because we had guests.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.050
I see.

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:46.480
"The Demon’s Banquet".

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:49.030
The poltergeist of Houshou Mitsuru!

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:54.660
Stop it, please!

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:31.690
What do you want, Bishounen Detective-kun?

00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:35.200
There’s something I'd like to ask you.

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:39.160
Don’t bother me; it makes the whiskey taste bad.

00:22:39.180 --> 00:22:43.960
Murasame-san, if you know anything
about Houshou Mitsuru, tell me.

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:49.590
If you don’t, you'll be killed.

00:22:56.280 --> 00:22:58.640
Where did Ryuu go?

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:02.310
Hey, doesn’t Ryuu-kun seem different from usual?

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:05.230
He’s been weird ever since he saw the Testa di Drago!

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:10.730
What?

00:23:10.760 --> 00:23:11.530
Let’s go!

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:22.080
How dare you!

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:25.500
What's going on?

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:56.170
Next Episode

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:52.090
The inheritors of the Testa di Drago
are under attack by Hell’s Maestro.

00:24:52.780 --> 00:24:55.800
The automatic murder trick is made clear!

00:24:55.820 --> 00:24:58.340
The truth of the genius violinist’s death.

00:24:58.370 --> 00:25:04.010
Can the Q-Class stop the melody of death
that echoes through the mansion?

00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:05.540
There’s one answer!

00:25:12.830 --> 00:25:14.490
I got left behind again.

00:25:19.850 --> 00:25:21.130
Well, I’m fine I guess.
